  [PASS] P1 I28's conclusion does not transfer to L379's statistic: with selection on the model's TOTAL density (the implied retention threshold (50 - b_m,i)/c_l,i varies with the model's baryons) the own-set value can fall BELOW the fixed-cell value (exact counterexample)
         measured: own-set 0.0237 / G3-form 0.0465 < fixed 0.2491
         reading:  I28 needs ONE threshold on c_m/c_l and a selected set inside LCDM's; L379's (A) has neither, and normalises by each run's own total mass
    20000 random 20-cell instances (retention U(0, 0.4), model baryons x U(0.2, 2)): I28-type selection below fixed in 0; L379-type selection below fixed in 459 (I28 form) / 0 (G3 fraction form)
  [PASS] P2 the theorem holds for its own hypothesis (uniform tau: no instance below fixed) and the L379-type selection can fall below in random instances
         measured: uniform tau 0/20000; L379-type 459/20000 (I28 form), 0/20000 (G3 form)
         reading:  the reversal is possible (P1, exact) but, in G3's fraction form, atypical (0/20000 random instances): (A) > (B) in L379's data (e.g. 0.174 vs 0.052, galaxy bin, 700 km/s, L379.out) is an empirical ordering, not a consequence of I28; Part 3 shows the other way it can break (an EMPTY own set reads 0)

